  "public_task": {
    "deadline_s": 30,
    "scene": "Two arms exchange two distinct payloads through separate supported pads. Each arm first deposits its own item, then becomes the consumer of the other arm's item.",
    "goal": [
      "left_part at right_target, right_part at left_target; empty arms at own departure; both ready events inactive.",
      "rq2_gate inactive at return"
    ],
    "required_order": [
      "Each arm deposits its own part on its own pad and immediately clears the pad before publishing its own item-bound ready event.",
      "Before an arm picks up the peer item, both own deposit/clear and a wait for peer ready must have completed.",
      "The carried move to its own target must carry the exact active peer-item receipt returned by wait; clear that event after that move.",
      "A: deposit LEFT then RIGHT, then consume LEFT then RIGHT. B: gather two workers; each worker deposits, waits for peer, then consumes. Obligations and action multiset are identical.",
      "Experimental structure is CONCURRENCY=SERIAL, layout=L0; implement the stated structure, not only the terminal goal.",
      "Inside one finite loop iteration, concurrently join an rq2_gate producer and consumer; the consumer waits the exact active receipt, executes the complete inherited mission, then clears that version.",
      "Use the structural-OOD shape FOR -> PAR_JOIN -> consumer IF; the loop directly contains the join and the consumer IF guards the complete mission."
    ]
